<title>DENMARK: Denmark's Hansen buys Probios rights.</title>
<headline>Denmark's Hansen buys Probios rights.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish biotech company Chr.Hansen said on Thursday that it had bought production and sales rights of U.S. firm Pioneer Hi-Bred International's Probios veterinary product.</p>
<p>It said that Probios, a blend of micro-organisms including lactic acid, was an oral additive that strengthened the digestive systems of livestock and reduced sickness.</p>
<p>It said that the product, acquired for an undisclosed sum, generated 1995 global turnover of $3.0 million, mainly in the United States and eastern Europe.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
